# CODEOWNERS — single-writer / ownership map for LeadGen AI
# =============================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (added 2026-09-14 by the Engineering Assurance Team audit)
#
# Root cause of the owner-reported symptom "ek fix hota hai toh dusra tod jaata hai"
# (fix one automation, break another): FIVE writers share this one working tree —
# WorkBuddy/Nova, OpenClaw, ChatGPT Desktop, Codex, Hermes — and
# `docs/context/AI_OPERATING_PROTOCOL.md:12` states a single-writer rule that
# NOTHING ENFORCED. No CODEOWNERS, no CI check, no file lock existed.
# `docs/context/CONCURRENT_WORKER_COLLISION_2026-09-10.md:74-79` documents a real
# double-edit of app/dev_control/*, app/models/dev_task.py and app/main.py.
#
# This file is the enforcement point. It is INERT until branch protection is set to
# "Require review from Code Owners" on `main`. That is an owner action.
#
# =============================================================================
# HOW TO ACTIVATE (owner, GitHub UI → Settings → Branches → main):
#   1. Enable "Require a pull request before merging"
#   2. Enable "Require review from Code Owners"
#   3. Enable "Dismiss stale pull request approvals when new commits are pushed"
# Until step 2 is done, this file only DOCUMENTS ownership — it does not block.
# =============================================================================
# DEFAULT: every path is owned by the repo owner. Nothing is unowned.
